INT. COUNTY SALT DOME - NIGHT

A cavern of road salt, pale as a glacier. A single work lamp hums on a tripod.

NGOZI ADEYEMI-BROOKS (50s, plow-crew foreman, reading glasses on a cord) stands over a clipboard. Around her: DEZ "THE DEACON" PRUITT (30s, enormous, soft-voiced), BILLIE WARSHAW (20s, rookie, hi-vis too big), TOMASZ KRÓL (60s, mechanic, grease to the elbow) and ARLO MENDES (40s, union steward, thermos in hand).

She taps the clipboard. They go quiet.

NGOZI
Listen up, all of you. The county cut the overnight run. Starting Friday.

Nobody moves. Tomasz sets down his wrench.

TOMASZ
Cut how.

NGOZI
Cut like gone.

ARLO
They can't. It's in the contract.

NGOZI
Arlo, it's in the contract that they can.

He looks at the thermos. Unscrews it. Doesn't pour.

BILLIE
So I just got here.

DEZ
Billie.

BILLIE
Three weeks. I bought boots.

DEZ
Billie, hush a second.

She does. He rests a hand on her shoulder, then thinks better of it and lets it drop.

TOMASZ
(to himself)
Thirty-one winters.

ARLO
I'll file tonight. Grievance, the whole thing. Ngozi, you sign as witness, Dez, you sign, Tomasz you sign, and Billie, you're probationary so you don't sign anything, you just watch.

BILLIE
That's not fair.

ARLO
No. It's not.

NGOZI
Nobody is filing anything tonight.

ARLO
Excuse me?

NGOZI
I took the deal.

Silence. Salt ticks somewhere in the dark as a small slide settles.

DEZ
What deal.

NGOZI
Day shift. Four of us stay. Two go.

ARLO
Who decides who goes.

NGOZI
I do.

TOMASZ
Then say it.

NGOZI
Tomasz, I'm not going to say it in front of the kids.

TOMASZ
I'm sixty-three years old. Say it.

She takes off her glasses. They drop on the cord against her chest.

NGOZI
You and Billie. Seniority says you, Tomasz, and last-hired says her, and I fought for it every other way and the number didn't move.

DEZ
You put me ahead of him?

NGOZI
I put nobody ahead of anybody. A spreadsheet did.

ARLO
A spreadsheet. Fantastic. I'll tell my wife I lost a man to a spreadsheet.

BILLIE
I can go. It's fine. I can go.

TOMASZ
Don't you dare say that's fine.

BILLIE
Then what do I say?

TOMASZ
Say you want to burn the place down.

BILLIE
I want to burn the place down.

TOMASZ
Good girl. Now say it like you mean it.

Dez laughs, a short bark, and that breaks it. Arlo laughs. Even Ngozi's mouth moves.

Then Tomasz is not laughing. He turns away toward the dark of the dome.

DEZ
Hey. Old man.

TOMASZ
(muttering)
Thirty-one winters, and a spreadsheet.

Ngozi puts her glasses back on, picks up the clipboard, and turns it to face them.

NGOZI
Everyone sign the grievance. Everyone. I'll sign first.

ARLO
You just said.

NGOZI
I said nobody files tonight. It's four a.m. We file at nine.

She signs. Passes it to Dez.
